# L §8.3 LOAD-UNIT `<a> and <b> have different units` (tally 2.1.6, issue #71): a row's literal is named with its
# unit, 100.00 EUR. tally 2.1.5's refcore printed the figure alone, `100.00 and money PLN`.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
input a: money PLN

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 100.00 EUR "plan"

ask q: a
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT 100.00 EUR and money PLN have different units (m.tally:16)
